---

## 1. Delegate Independent Lookups — Fan-Out

Use a **workflow with `AddFanOutEdge`** to broadcast the same input to multiple agents concurrently. The framework provides `ConcurrentStartExecutor` as a built-in starting point:

```csharp
var physicist = new ChatClientAgent(chatClient, name: "Physicist",
    instructions: "You are an expert in physics...")
    .BindAsExecutor(new AIAgentHostOptions { ForwardIncomingMessages = false });

var chemist = new ChatClientAgent(chatClient, name: "Chemist",
    instructions: "You are an expert in chemistry...")
    .BindAsExecutor(new AIAgentHostOptions { ForwardIncomingMessages = false });

var startExecutor = new ConcurrentStartExecutor();

var workflow = new WorkflowBuilder(startExecutor)
    .AddFanOutEdge(startExecutor, [physicist, chemist])   // ← fan-out
    .AddFanInBarrierEdge([physicist, chemist], aggregationExecutor) // ← fan-in
    .WithOutputFrom(aggregationExecutor)
    .Build();
```

`ConcurrentStartExecutor` broadcasts a `ChatMessage` to all connected agents, then sends a `TurnToken` to kick them off simultaneously (`dotnet/src/Microsoft.Agents.AI.Workflows/Specialized/ConcurrentStartExecutor.cs`).

---

## 2. Wait for All Results — Fan-In Barrier

The `AddFanInBarrierEdge` ensures the aggregation executor doesn't run until **every** fan-out agent has completed. Internally, `ConcurrentEndExecutor` tracks remaining inputs with a counter:

```csharp
// ConcurrentEndExecutor.cs (lines 41-59)
bool done;
lock (this._allResults)
{
    this._allResults.Add(messages);
    done = --this._remaining == 0;
}

if (done)
{
    var results = this._allResults;
    this._allResults = new List<List<ChatMessage>>(this._expectedInputs);
    await context.YieldOutputAsync(this._aggregator(results), cancellationToken);
}
```

Your aggregation executor receives `List<ChatMessage>` from each agent and combines them. Override `OnMessageDeliveryFinishedAsync` to finalize after all deliveries complete:

```csharp
[YieldsOutput(typeof(string))]
internal sealed partial class AggregationExecutor() :
    Executor<List<ChatMessage>>("AggregationExecutor")
{
    private readonly List<ChatMessage> _messages = [];

    public override async ValueTask HandleAsync(List<ChatMessage> message, IWorkflowContext context, CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        this._messages.AddRange(message);
    }

    protected override ValueTask OnMessageDeliveryFinishedAsync(IWorkflowContext context, CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        var result = string.Join("\n---\n", this._messages.Select(m => $"{m.AuthorName}: {m.Text}"));
        this._messages.Clear();
        return context.YieldOutputAsync(result, ct);
    }
}
```

